# Dead Letter Vault archive stacks. Format: see "Floor layouts" in AGENTS.md.
# World units, the same axes as engine.rs: screen-right is +x+y, screen-down is +x-y.
floor vault_stacks
# Design px of the baked image: width, height, then where world (0, 0, 0) lands.
image 2080 1440 250 760
bounds 0 0 20 16
entrance 1.0 2.0 1 0
landmark 8.425 6.55

# Far walls: the back of the cutaway, tall. Entrance in the left wall between y 1.0 and 3.0.
block wall -0.6 -0.6 0 1.0 3.8
block wall -0.6 3.0 0 16.6 3.8
block wall 0 16 11.6 16.6 3.8
block wall 13.4 16 15.2 16.6 3.8
block wall 17.0 16 20.6 16.6 3.8
# Near walls, cut down.
block wall 0 -0.6 20.6 0 0.4
block wall 20 0 20.6 16 0.4
# West ranks terminate in a chained register bay, visible over the first rank.
block stack 0 3.4 7.0 4.4 3.6
block stack 0 6.2 7.0 7.2 3.6
block stack 0 8.4 9.7 9.4 3.6
block stack 0 11.8 5.4 12.8 3.6
block stack 0 14.4 5.4 15.4 3.6
block railing 9.7 3.4 9.9 9.4 0.8
# North ranks and the cordoned-off records reserve beyond the cross-aisle.
block stack 6.0 11.0 6.8 16 3.6
block stack 7.6 11.0 8.4 16 3.6
block landmark 7.15 5.1 9.7 8.0 4.9
block railing 5.6 10.8 12.4 11.0 0.8
block railing 12.2 11.0 12.4 14.0 0.8
# Sectioned stacks between the cross-aisle and the front aisle.
block stack 7.0 3.4 9.7 4.4 0.8
block stack 11.0 3.6 12.0 7.6 0.8
block stack 13.6 3.6 14.6 7.6 0.8
block stack 16.2 3.6 17.2 7.6 0.8
# Cropped sorting cabinet on the approach to the stop door.
block stack 15.0 10.4 17.6 11.2 0.8

# Encounter entrances at the junction. Crossing `stop` starts the chamber.
door side 11.7 15.2 13.3 16
door stop 15.3 15.2 16.9 16

route main 1.0 2.0 10.5 2.0 10.5 9.9 13.2 9.9 14.2 12.6 16.1 14.0 16.1 15.6
route loop 13.2 9.9 18.6 9.9 18.6 2.0 10.5 2.0
route side 13.2 9.9 14.2 12.6 12.9 14.2 12.9 15.6

view arrival 5.0 2.0
view junction 13.05 9.65
view return 10.5 2.0
